  "workflows": [],
  "tools": [
    "tool:watch-my-sources",
    "tool:pour-example-rows-into-my-list"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    "1. Make list:signal-sources from the example rows, or pour them into the list of sites you already follow (see pour). Mark a place Yes in Watching to have it read; starter places are made turned off. A new list:signals and list:ranked-items are made by the tool itself when needed.",
    "2. Say \"Watch my sources\". The AI calls run_resource_operation at @workshop-tools with method tools:run and tool tool:watch-my-sources with input {} (the first worked example shows it). The first read of a source is a quiet baseline: it keeps what is there and moves nothing.",
    "3. On a later run, when new items wait, the answer carries weigh_wanted: one question {purpose, identity, messages, max_tokens} listing your pursuits and the new items. Answer it yourself as your AI with the JSON {\"items\": [{n, link, moves, how, format, why}]} and nothing else, then run the tool again with weighed {identity, reply}.",
    "4. Read the answer: read (sources read), kept (new items kept), moves (items that move a pursuit, with the pursuit and how), set_aside, waiting and problems (a source that failed, with its name). Hand each entry of arrivals to your arrival door exactly as it is. Tell the person the moves; the rest is in their Signals list.",
    "5. Run it again on a schedule (hourly) or when the person asks what is new. It sends nothing outward and never writes to a source."
  ],
  "worked_examples": [
    {
      "title": "A blog's two new posts wait to be weighed",
      "ask": "Watch my sources and tell me what is new.",
      "mcp": {
        "server": "trillion",
        "tool": "run_resource_operation",
        "input": {
          "address": "@workshop-tools",
          "method": "tools:run",
          "input": {
            "tool": "tool:watch-my-sources",
            "input": {}
          }
        }
      },
      "given": "From tools/watch-my-sources/test/watch-my-sources.test.mjs, run for real on its made-up world: list:signal-sources holds the row blog (The Blog, feed https://blog.example/feed.xml, kind feed, Watching Yes, last read 2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z); the feed has the posts 'Booking podcast guests' and 'Ten tax tips'; the pursuit pursuit:podcast is 'Launch the podcast', after: 'Publish weekly'.",
      "hands_back": "{\"read\":1,\"kept\":2,\"ranked\":0,\"moves\":[],\"set_aside\":0,\"waiting\":2,\"problems\":[],\"sources_waiting\":0,\"arrivals\":[],\"weigh_wanted\":{\"purpose\":\"signal-weigh\",\"identity\":\"1f:7247061cccf15715b65d148c482c0fbf2be0283b73b7b27c2a8cc2b497f21e8a\",\"max_tokens\":1500,\"messages\":[...]}}. The last message lists the pursuit 'pursuit:podcast | Launch the podcast | after: Publish weekly' and numbers the items: 1 Ten tax tips, 2 Booking podcast guests, each with its link."
    },
    {
      "title": "The AI answers the question and one post moves the podcast",
      "ask": "Here is my answer to the weighing question; finish the run.",
      "mcp": {
        "server": "trillion",
        "tool": "run_resource_operation",
        "input": {
          "address": "@workshop-tools",
          "method": "tools:run",
          "input": {
            "tool": "tool:watch-my-sources",
            "input": {
              "weighed": {
                "identity": "1f:7247061cccf15715b65d148c482c0fbf2be0283b73b7b27c2a8cc2b497f21e8a",
                "reply": "{\"items\":[{\"n\":1,\"link\":\"https://blog.example/tax\",\"moves\":null,\"how\":null,\"format\":null,\"why\":\"It shares a word, nothing more.\"},{\"n\":2,\"link\":\"https://blog.example/guests\",\"moves\":\"pursuit:podcast\",\"how\":\"direct\",\"format\":null,\"why\":\"It is about booking guests.\"}]}"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "given": "The same run, an hour later, answered with the identity of the question above (read from the test and observed by running it).",
      "hands_back": "{\"read\":1,\"kept\":0,\"ranked\":0,\"moves\":[{\"title\":\"Booking podcast guests\",\"link\":\"https://blog.example/guests\",\"pursuit\":\"pursuit:podcast\",\"how\":\"direct\"}],\"set_aside\":1,\"waiting\":0,\"problems\":[],\"sources_waiting\":0,\"arrivals\":[{\"route\":\"watch-sources\",\"source_id\":\"https://blog.example/guests\",\"from_person\":false,\"title\":\"Booking podcast guests\",\"from\":\"The Blog\",\"text\":\"The Blog: Booking podcast guests\\nIt is about booking guests.\\nhttps://blog.example/guests\",\"at\":\"2026-10-07T07:00:00.000Z\"}]}. The post 'Ten tax tips' is set aside; the signals rows end as Moves a pursuit and Set aside."
    }
  ],
